# `pluss::subsp::stats::ts::AdfOptions`

Options of `ts::adf_test`.

`AdfOptions` chooses the deterministic terms and the augmentation of the test regression.

## Fields

| Field | Type | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lags` | `std::int64_t` | 0 | Lagged changes added to absorb short-run dynamics (the 'augmented' part); each uses up an observation. |
| `model` | `ts::AdfModel` | `ARD` | `AR`: no deterministic term. `ARD`: a constant. `TS`: a constant and a linear trend. |
| `alpha` | `double` | 0.05 | Significance level of the critical value and of `reject`. |

## Guidance

The defaults are a sensible starting point; change a field only for the reason its row gives.

